> Well that was the rule, for years! =A0No one was allowed to speak
> Lojban. =A0Not without weathering severe criticism, anyway!

What rule? When? I've been speaking Lojban since a couple of weeks
after I started learning it, and nobody has ever told me I couldn't do
it. And of course I have made my good share of mistakes.

I guess the difference between "severe criticism" and "helpful
corrections" has to do as much with the giver as with the receiver.
Not everybody is always extremely polite, and some people are too
thin-skinned, what can you do?

> I hear it was even worse before I was involved, like the Loglan days.
> I read something the other day about how everyone sent their attempts
> at Loglan to JCB, and he just didn't send them on to anyone else
> because he didn't think they were good enough, they were all just
> hidden away, and like one person wrote a text and published it anyway
> but JCB was furious! =A0Is that really what it was like, oldbies?

Something like that, yes, I hear he had to FTC everything
(fine-tooth-comb), but that was long before Al Gore invented the
internets. Nothing like that ever went on with Lojban.

